commit e9628d54ba92197e5baf39a15c14556481001094
cli/neo: add --print/-p for non-interactive one-shot prompts

Adds `pulumi neo -p "<prompt>"` for AI-agent interop: run a single prompt,
execute CLI tool calls locally, and print the agent's final response to
stdout (status to stderr).

Session learns an Output writer that, when set, captures the Content of
the first IsFinal=true assistant_message with no pending CLI tool calls
and ends Run via an errSessionDone sentinel — the SSE stream never closes
on its own. The non-interactive prompt is wrapped with a brief preamble
telling Neo it's running headless so it doesn't ask follow-up questions.

--print + --approval-mode=manual is rejected at flag-parse time (no UI to
approve from); when unset, --print defaults approval to auto.

Fixes pulumi/pulumi-service#43402

